    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Note that the solution of Equations 26.3 and 26.4 requires the inverse of the covariance matrix V. In the preceding example, $ V^{-1} $ was not particularly difficult to obtain. However, when y contains many thousands of observations, as is commonly the case in cattle breeding, the computation of $ V^{-1} $ can be quite difficult. As a way around this problem, Henderson (1950, 1963, 1973, 1984a)",
